[{:db/id "q-70895/selection/daf1bcada75fb602dc1b3f02a0b837b1a34a78cb5662477766e206716c7f4069" :answer/id #uuid "1f8bfae0-3eba-5472-81af-441df8800e08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895/selection/af572c87cd56a2b2fa54758f9a2e220056d2501a59ff8a6d67b900dc56854051" :answer/id #uuid "dc507dbf-7cc3-56d5-823b-08d241c9a062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=⟨3,-5,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895/selection/5bfd81fddd8ffd5effa2bf43519340226f193652639b80b1b2d24d5682a5962a" :answer/id #uuid "4ed6607f-2a3f-5645-9a9a-7de309608bb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=⟨-3,4,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895/selection/c7cd9fd73046c540b16628337352a2c75672666e7e35803bece09761ad4b2448" :answer/id #uuid "e945a2ae-a784-5e25-88a2-b730d398b06f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895/selection/bca3c1a6c93a5c96657434760a3de87e1d108c9fd1d7ea516d4798d75d15caac" :answer/id #uuid "05672043-2125-5a7b-a7cb-f67a390bfb2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6b8fc01-b722-5332-8a4b-09309993af92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70895/selection/daf1bcada75fb602dc1b3f02a0b837b1a34a78cb5662477766e206716c7f4069" :answer-field/choices ["q-70895/selection/daf1bcada75fb602dc1b3f02a0b837b1a34a78cb5662477766e206716c7f4069" "q-70895/selection/af572c87cd56a2b2fa54758f9a2e220056d2501a59ff8a6d67b900dc56854051" "q-70895/selection/5bfd81fddd8ffd5effa2bf43519340226f193652639b80b1b2d24d5682a5962a" "q-70895/selection/c7cd9fd73046c540b16628337352a2c75672666e7e35803bece09761ad4b2448" "q-70895/selection/bca3c1a6c93a5c96657434760a3de87e1d108c9fd1d7ea516d4798d75d15caac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70895" :question/id #uuid "ca2b2271-1ec0-5a3e-b5ac-687d91668797" :question/math-academy-id "q-70895" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-5,-2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,3,4⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-70895/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70895"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "aed5ce7a-ce77-563e-a120-802fb7c3c0e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "49147c48-3c79-59ef-85df-0ae687ad910c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "43c20240-428f-5295-ac13-745401af8941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "5b1511a1-0592-5e16-ae3d-355dbe352c92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51cbf961-880f-5565-ab09-ae794ec61fcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127873/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-127873/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-127873/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-127873/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-127873/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-127873/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127873" :question/id #uuid "401ba6bc-fa27-5ba0-acab-8c53d45558b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127873" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127873/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "89f6d816-5381-5306-b4c9-c34c049885d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "be7da4de-0848-51fe-be88-efe52ae6412b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "41eae54d-3456-5113-9d8b-1c7ace24b718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "a7e21bff-5775-520e-aa3f-3af78aec6c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "331a3a0d-e903-59b3-9147-23a3def27b44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eafa7ebb-6b96-5c3c-a7ed-5307588cc416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127910/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-127910/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-127910/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-127910/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-127910/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-127910/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127910" :question/id #uuid "05136695-9e80-59ef-a336-fc6a855ca97f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127910" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & ={t}_{2}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨3,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127910/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127910"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection/2252a735d6a8dee277c92b2c58b79b3de3007011b8bb2710b0ba4a7dfdecd5e0" :answer/id #uuid "06b379fd-7d70-5e49-8081-a3b64f84134e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection/b4fcfc7491ed138e420f6a1bfc52caa18eb0fe2fa277914cf83e44dc9cf94a53" :answer/id #uuid "56439333-b485-5577-b3fc-2b0a4fb30508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection/3cad3c4e61f3140746dac22227fdd119b676d6c857c8e1b99b88dcd8c7e900d3" :answer/id #uuid "0d2c1c27-eb96-5b3b-9be4-85fc3ed5d870" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection/c1b9b7481ae38b80a76aeb9c5b4954be256ce6e3f849653dff5a40e515f3e143" :answer/id #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection/6d719c2a9392e50fc0d6511e0216f51ec5e0e012e600f7001b9ad792c03a9e34" :answer/id #uuid "18790217-0164-5be5-8309-2e02c079a999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea1771e-337a-53ba-af67-134749c7dc53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127927/selection/c1b9b7481ae38b80a76aeb9c5b4954be256ce6e3f849653dff5a40e515f3e143" :answer-field/choices ["q-127927/selection/2252a735d6a8dee277c92b2c58b79b3de3007011b8bb2710b0ba4a7dfdecd5e0" "q-127927/selection/b4fcfc7491ed138e420f6a1bfc52caa18eb0fe2fa277914cf83e44dc9cf94a53" "q-127927/selection/3cad3c4e61f3140746dac22227fdd119b676d6c857c8e1b99b88dcd8c7e900d3" "q-127927/selection/c1b9b7481ae38b80a76aeb9c5b4954be256ce6e3f849653dff5a40e515f3e143" "q-127927/selection/6d719c2a9392e50fc0d6511e0216f51ec5e0e012e600f7001b9ad792c03a9e34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127927" :question/id #uuid "5fb6c451-3fd1-5933-bfd5-1dcab52c2777" :question/math-academy-id "q-127927" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127927/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection/4339e929472c1e1a6c30652256a894de8dfc6902fc206ab35319356e551e9025" :answer/id #uuid "97b1a154-e6ea-5ad5-bc67-985ac790249f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection/d3d041f311a17465fadefb7ff10d371541bc0a0e32b49eeb2b9a0cbd0a2de585" :answer/id #uuid "facf8c4b-8e3d-5a24-a63e-b12fc172190e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection/7ff49eb0c2cf9e70f6b4038a4c4639b7daf6bfdf29ece8ffbab3f04f79542e87" :answer/id #uuid "c19bf435-7bb8-561f-ba12-0c791dd434be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection/11b4c8235e157a8bace23a1c353dc86a044f02c69598d886e967265544493e2e" :answer/id #uuid "24d09d6d-587a-5131-bf7b-17c4a5299f8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection/8c462eb2ffd538856573a15f79c00137571c4b03845c54997c421a78ee7c05af" :answer/id #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c8d44ee-444f-5365-a1c8-4d6392e75dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127948/selection/8c462eb2ffd538856573a15f79c00137571c4b03845c54997c421a78ee7c05af" :answer-field/choices ["q-127948/selection/4339e929472c1e1a6c30652256a894de8dfc6902fc206ab35319356e551e9025" "q-127948/selection/d3d041f311a17465fadefb7ff10d371541bc0a0e32b49eeb2b9a0cbd0a2de585" "q-127948/selection/7ff49eb0c2cf9e70f6b4038a4c4639b7daf6bfdf29ece8ffbab3f04f79542e87" "q-127948/selection/11b4c8235e157a8bace23a1c353dc86a044f02c69598d886e967265544493e2e" "q-127948/selection/8c462eb2ffd538856573a15f79c00137571c4b03845c54997c421a78ee7c05af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127948" :question/id #uuid "0063bd61-9495-5b7f-ae6d-384a92c58a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-127948" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127948/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
